# Fast, build-free checks only. Everything heavier — the build, typecheck, the
# test suites, surface:check, the website build and the bundle-size budgets —
# runs in CI, in the "Verify" and "Size limit" steps of
# `.github/workflows/test.yml`.
#
# Know exactly when that is: `test.yml` triggers on pull requests targeting
# main and on pushes to main — NOT on a push to a feature branch. So while no
# pull request is open, a push is covered by this hook and nothing else. That
# is the real trade here; nothing below used to be checked *only* locally, but
# it is now checked *later*, and not at all until you open the pull request.
#
# This hook is deliberately small for two reasons, and the first one is not a
# preference:
#
#   1. A long hook breaks the push outright. git connects to the remote and
#      reads the ref advertisement *before* running pre-push — that is how this
#      hook receives refs on stdin. So everything below runs while the server's
#      receive-pack sits idle, and past its timeout the push dies with SIGPIPE
#      (exit 141) with every check green. `pnpm verify` is ~2 min warm and ~7
#      min cold, which was reliably over the line. SSH keepalives do not help:
#      they keep the transport alive, not the server's receive-pack.
#
#   2. `pnpm verify` runs the whole test suite on the developer's machine, but
#      CI's verify matrix is ubuntu + macos only. A Windows-fragile test (a
#      tight timing bound, usually) therefore blocks the push locally while
#      passing CI — see issue #162.
#
# Both checks below run without a build, which is what keeps them fast:
# eslint here is deliberately non-type-checked (see eslint.config.mjs), and
# prettier reads source. surface:check and typecheck are NOT in this set —
# both need built workspace packages, which is the expensive part.
#
# Before pushing anything substantial, run the real gate yourself:
#   pnpm verify && pnpm size-limit
#
# Skip this hook in emergencies with `git push --no-verify`.
pnpm format:check
pnpm lint
